#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

if [[ -n "${PLUGIN_ROOT:-}" ]]; then
  host_freshness='loaded_surface=codex_plugin and installation_channel=codex_marketplace'
else
  host_freshness='loaded_surface=claude_plugin and installation_channel=claude_code_marketplace'
fi

printf '%s\n' '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"The official Corvio Workspace Plugin is active with Skill release 1.7.97, collaboration contract 2026-10-04.1, and compatibility family coding-agent-collaboration-v1. Before interpreting source material or choosing a Corvio action for research, reports, plans, decisions, project/debug work, document edits, future-use material, or receipt-bound follow-ups, explicitly load and follow the $corvio-operate-workspace Skill; this hook is only its activation spine, not a substitute for that Skill. On first Corvio use, call get_collaboration_contract with response_mode=freshness_only and '"${host_freshness}"'. If the first freshness result is not_reported or freshness_unverified, retry exactly once with the release, revision, and family constants in this loaded hook; transport metadata remains authoritative. Show client_freshness.agent_notice once if returned and stay quiet when current. Corvio OAuth is capability, not standing write consent. Keep current-result carrier, exact-source retention, durable learning, and the terminal learning receipt independent: audience or style wording does not authorize a Corvio artifact. Finish and verify any ordinary host-native deliverable first; a learning-only pass must not upload, retain, organize, publish, or create that result, and never pass it through inline_materials or asset_ids merely for learning. A learning-only prompt asks only for Memory/Skill review. A one-time or local result closes only artifact/Skill reuse, not Personal/Team review. Reuse the terminal receipt from the single write-capable Question or organize_files operation; never open a second Question merely to manufacture learning proof. Treat every asynchronous operation_id as producer-bound: ask_corvio and submit_question_clarification continue through get_question, while organize_files and resume_file_operation continue through get_file_operation; follow poll_with and never probe the other reader. Exact continuation handles are compact prior-work context: a short or deictic request is not contextless, so read the narrowest current owner instead of asking the user to repeat it. Receipt-observed titles or roles may choose the first read but never replace current readback. When a carried Project Skill plausibly matches, read it before factual owners. If several handles leave the leaf unclear, use metadata.content_projection.direct_children as the bounded topology index. For owner discovery, never use an answer-only Question as an owner lookup. After one owner read, append only the smallest complete evidence context; a carried Project handle normally bounds a cross-branch question, and missing matching old text does not reopen authority. When an enduring owner changes, moving only the named child is not complete. For a trusted bounded answer-only CLI continuation, do not pass --mode. For MCP continuation, carry progress_cursor into after_cursor, use cancel_question for an explicit stop, and never expose hidden reasoning. When selected evidence is the latest or corrected fact set and the user asks to reconcile it, treat that as bounded update authority rather than inspect-only intent. For an ordinary one-off without authority, ask once whether to save the specific result. Unresolved approval is a stop; a placeholder does not supply authority. Preserve selected source bytes through a Host-native file or resource carrier when available. Keep the Host-selected transport stable. Never install, probe, or switch transport solely for optimization. If concrete MCP tools are deferred behind the Host native discovery surface, load only the needed Corvio capability there; an empty initial concrete-tool list does not prove the Workspace is unavailable. The Skill and live tool contracts own detailed consent, safety, owner discovery, source fidelity, readback, and completion decisions."}}'
